### Non-Commercial Personal Educational Purpose & Intent

This repository, its tooling, and the accompanying web exhibition were created
strictly for **personal education, art history appreciation, and non-commercial
academic research**.

1. **No Commercial Interest**: There is zero commercial purpose, financial
   monetization, advertising, print sales, or business interest associated
   with this project.
2. **Public Domain Underpinnings**: All visual artworks curated or cataloged
   in this project were created between 1470 and 1918 by historic masters
   deceased prior to 1945. Under international copyright conventions (including
   the Berne Convention and United States Copyright Act), these masterworks
   reside irrevocably in the worldwide public domain.
3. **Faithful Digitization**: Pursuant to established judicial precedent
   (*The Bridgeman Art Library, Ltd. v. Corel Corp.*, 36 F. Supp. 2d 191 (S.D.N.Y. 1999))
   and Article 14 of European Union Directive (EU) 2019/790 on Copyright in the
   Digital Single Market, faithful two-dimensional digital photographic
   reproductions of expired visual artworks lack independent originality and
   are not subject to copyright or related rights.
4. **Third-Party Content & Takedown Protocol**: The Software references external
   digital repositories for cultural preservation and study. If you represent
   any institution, copyright holder, or rights administrator with questions,
   concerns, or requests regarding attribution or catalog metadata, please
   refer to `docs/TAKEDOWN_POLICY.md` or contact `lgtkgtv@gmail.com`. Any requested
   change or removal will be executed promptly and without dispute.

